{
  // PvE-specific corrections.
  //
  // Entries below are ACTIVE: tarkov.dev currently serves a wrong value for PvE
  // and these correct it. True per-mode values live in
  // src/divergences/tasks.json5, which is what `npm run check-overrides` uses
  // to detect a mirror-direction flip; superseded overrides are removed and
  // recoverable from git history.

  // REMOVED: the Season 1 patch replaced player-level quest
  // requirements with trader loyalty levels, so minPlayerLevel no longer
  // applies to quests generally (confirmed against the 1.1-pve data:
  // none of the formerly-divergent quests carry a Level condition). Collector
  // is the exception - see its entry below for the surviving 1.1-pve
  // minPlayerLevel divergence (40 vs regular's 42).

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // EFT 1.1.0.0 quest experience rework - PvE values from the 1.1-pve data,
  // cross-checked against tarkov.dev. These tasks
  // still diverge from regular per the wiki (which documents PvP): the wiki
  // backs the value tarkov.dev serves for regular, while the 1.1-pve data proves PvE
  // now awards the new value. The wiki pages simply have not been updated to
  // 1.1 values yet, so the pair is recorded as divergent in
  // src/divergences/tasks.json5 - if a PvP capture later confirms regular also
  // changed, move these to base and converge the registry entries.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // Surveillance - PvE experience reworked in 1.1.0.0
